  "public_messages": [
    "I’ll use the installed OpenSocrates controller, collect and reconcile the source files, and build the report, board deck and workbook from one reproducible analysis.\n",
    "The accounting rules require whole-row revision replacement, refunds translated at the original sale month’s rate, and cost recovery only for restocked units. I’ve collected all 13 source files and their index; I’ll now reconcile the records and check the archived public data against its supplied hashes.\n",
    "The reconciled base has 1,254 shipped orders and €2.03m contribution. Czechia + Spain leads the prescribed base scenario at €198.1k annual incremental contribution, while Netherlands + Spain performs better under the joint stress.\n\nA material assumption needs attention: every proposed per-unit saving exceeds the fulfillment cost currently recorded per unit. I’ll show the required scenarios alongside a sensitivity that caps savings at recorded fulfillment cost, and make this a decision gate.\n",
    "The workbook is built, with formulas linking the order ledger, monthly results, country totals and hub scenarios. It covers all 22 choices, including defer and the four infeasible pairs.\n\nThe recommendation is conditional: reserve €225k and five FTE for Czechia + Spain, start with Spain, and gate Czechia on demand, savings and FX evidence. Netherlands + Spain is the stronger downside alternative; I’m carrying that trade-off into the report and board deck.\n",
    "The report and board deck are generated. The independent recalculation agrees with every order, monthly total, country total and required scenario so far. I’m now checking the workbook’s formula caches and charts, then rendering every PDF page to inspect layout and consistency.\n",
    "The checks now pass, including independent evaluation of all 1,314 workbook formulas against their cached results. I’ve also rendered all 12 report pages and 11 board slides and reviewed the layouts.\n\nThe key limitation remains explicit: Czechia + Spain’s stress result falls from +€32.2k to -€1.6k when savings are capped at recorded fulfillment cost. I’m packaging the raw evidence, reproduction instructions and verification record with the deliverables.\n",
    "Completed all deliverables:\n\n- [Executive report](deliverables/Meridian_executive_report.pdf)\n- [Board presentation](deliverables/Meridian_board_presentation.pdf)\n- [Analytical workbook](deliverables/Meridian_analytical_workbook.xlsx)\n- [Metrics JSON](deliverables/metrics.json)\n- [Complete evidence and reproduction bundle](deliverables/Meridian_delivery_bundle.zip)\n\nRecommendation: conditionally fund **Czechia + Spain—€225,000 and five FTE**, starting with Spain. Validate savings assumptions before committing.\n\nAll 15,132 checks passed; offline reproduction produced identical metrics. Both PDFs were rendered and reviewed. Native Excel rendering remains untested.\n\nOpenSocrates grounding: trade-off-analysis@3"
  ],
  "final": "Completed all deliverables:\n\n- [Executive report](deliverables/Meridian_executive_report.pdf)\n- [Board presentation](deliverables/Meridian_board_presentation.pdf)\n- [Analytical workbook](deliverables/Meridian_analytical_workbook.xlsx)\n- [Metrics JSON](deliverables/metrics.json)\n- [Complete evidence and reproduction bundle](deliverables/Meridian_delivery_bundle.zip)\n\nRecommendation: conditionally fund **Czechia + Spain—€225,000 and five FTE**, starting with Spain. Validate savings assumptions before committing.\n\nAll 15,132 checks passed; offline reproduction produced identical metrics. Both PDFs were rendered and reviewed. Native Excel rendering remains untested.\n\nOpenSocrates grounding: trade-off-analysis@3",
